      "description": "Builds formal/ with lake: every theorem of formal/Exegra/ type-checks, and the #guard_msgs axiom checks fail the build on sorryAx or a non-standard axiom; no Lean source uses sorry or admit or declares an axiom. Skipped, with a message, when lake is not on the PATH."
    },
    {
      "id": "ev-formal-explore",
      "claim": "exhaustive-exploration-sound",
      "kind": "test",
      "ref": "tests/proofs/formal-explore.test.js",
      "description": "exegra prove on the race fixture: the lost update is a counterexample accepted by Lean, its scripted run passes the trace check, the atomic store holds for all N configurations with the same N on two runs, and its precedes claim holds on every complete run. Skipped, with a message, when lake is not on the PATH."
    },
    {
      "id": "ev-formal-explore-bounded",
      "claim": "invariants-proved-within-bounds",
      "kind": "test",
      "ref": "tests/proofs/formal-explore.test.js#the atomic store is verified for every reachable configuration",
      "description": "exegra prove reports the atomic store's invariant as holding with method lean-exhaustive, the bound and N, after Lean accepted the theorem in the generated file. Skipped, with a message, when lake is not on the PATH."
    },
    {
      "id": "ev-formal-explore-temporal",
      "claim": "temporal-claims-checked-on-all-runs",
      "kind": "test",
      "ref": "tests/proofs/formal-explore.test.js#temporal claims: eventually holds",
      "description": "exegra prove on the race fixture: an eventually holds on every path; an eventually fails with a counterexample run that drops the event and ends without it; a precedes that the scripted run satisfies is violated by a run that reorders simultaneous events. Skipped, with a message, when lake is not on the PATH."
    },
    {
      "id": "ev-lean-boundary",
      "claim": "lean-boundary-errors-are-values",
      "kind": "test",
      "ref": "tests/core/lean.test.js",
      "description": "Calls through src/core/lean.js: the registry lists engine.run, an unknown function, a malformed request and refused arguments come back as errors, and a run returns the trace the engine returns."
    },
    {
      "id": "ev-lean-core-browser",
      "claim": "lean-core-runs-in-browser",
      "kind": "test",
      "ref": "tests/browser/lean-core.spec.js",
      "description": "In Chrome: the page loads the Lean core through src/core/lean.js, lists its functions, gets an error value for an unknown function and reproduces two golden traces."
